## Objective (designed by the tester)

Prove that the AT-x960-56YSQ's built-in **Local RADIUS Server** can be enabled and configured
with a NAS client and local users; that it then answers real RADIUS Access-Requests on the
wire with Access-Accept for a valid user and Access-Reject for an invalid one; that each reply
is cryptographically bound to the configured shared secret; that requests from a host that is
not a configured NAS, and requests carrying the wrong shared secret, are NOT accepted; and
that the whole configuration can be removed and leaves the running-config as it was found.

Baseline-OFF first, then ON, then the controls, then removal (`satisfactory-level-of-testing`).

