## Instruments (written for this campaign, committed to tools/ with README entries)

    tools/radius.py   RADIUS codec: header, attributes, PAP hide/unhide, Request and Response
                      Authenticators, Message-Authenticator. `python3 radius.py` self-tests it
                      (run on tb277: "radius.py self-test: OK").
    tools/radsend.py  a NAS in one command: sends Access-Request / Accounting-Request and
                      VERIFIES the reply's Response Authenticator against the shared secret.
    tools/radsrv.py   a pure-Python RADIUS server on unprivileged ports (used by T33408/T33409).
    tools/radwire.py  decodes and COUNTS the RADIUS packets in a tcpdump pcap, and verifies
                      each reply's authenticator -- the wire half of the evidence
                      (STANDING-ORDERS §7). Reuses snmpwire.py's pcap/Ethernet/UDP walk.

All four were end-to-end tested against each other on the dev host before any bench use
(Accept, wrong-password Reject, unknown-user Reject, wrong-secret, Accounting-Start).

## STEP 1 (designed) -- baseline with the feature OFF: the DUT must NOT answer RADIUS

Expected (designed): with no Local RADIUS Server configured, UDP/1812 on the DUT's vlan10
address is closed, and an Access-Request sent to it gets no RADIUS reply.

Capture (box): tools/tb capture tb277 ckaaa eth3 20 t33407-off.pcap udp and port 1812 or port
1813 or port 11812 or port 11813

Send (box, as the NAS):

    tools/tb tool tb277 ckaaa radsend 10.38.22.34 --port 1812 --secret testing123 \
        --user testuser --password testing123 --bind 10.38.22.33 --timeout 3 --retries 1

    -> Access-Request id=113 to 10.38.22.34:1812 from 10.38.22.33  User-Name='testuser',
       User-Password=<hidden,16 bytes>, NAS-IP-Address=10.38.22.33, NAS-Port=0,
       NAS-Port-Type=5, Service-Type=1(Login)
    <- NO REPLY after 3.0s (x2)  [ICMP port unreachable: nothing listening on that UDP port]
    radsend: sent=1 replies=0 no_reply=1 rejects=0 bad_authenticator=0      (exit 1)

Wire (tools/tb tool tb277 ckaaa radwire /tmp/ckaaa/t33407-off.pcap --secret testing123):

       0.000  10.38.22.33:34026 -> 10.38.22.34:1812  Access-Request id=49  len=72
      14.192  10.38.22.33:38368 -> 10.38.22.34:1812  Access-Request id=113 len=72
      14.192  10.38.22.33:38368 -> 10.38.22.34:1812  Access-Request id=113 len=72
    radwire: 3 RADIUS packet(s) in /tmp/ckaaa/t33407-off.pcap
      Access-Request         3
      authenticator check: valid=0 invalid=0 unpaired=0

**3 Access-Requests left the box, 0 RADIUS packets came back.** The DUT answered ICMP
port-unreachable instead, which is a positive proof that no process on the DUT is bound to
UDP/1812 -- stronger than silence, because silence could also be a lost packet.
STEP 1 verdict: PASS (the OFF baseline is established at frame level).

